From: Local Patches <patches@local>
Date: Fri, 24 Jan 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fftools: force DTS monotonicity with shared PCR offset (V3 - anti-oscillation)

This patch maintains DTS monotonicity across timestamp discontinuities
in live streams while preserving A/V synchronization.

V3 Changes (anti-oscillation fix):
- Backward jumps larger than the forward threshold (30s by default) are now
  recognized as source timeline resets and NOT corrected
- This prevents the offset from oscillating wildly between large positive
  and negative values, which caused catastrophic A/V desync
- Filter-level discontinuity handling (patch 0009) deals with resulting
  stale buffered frames

V2 Changes (shared PCR offset):
- Uses a single shared reference offset based on PCR stream (or video fallback)
- All streams receive the same correction, maintaining perfect A/V sync
- Eliminates the per-stream offset drift issue from V1

New command-line options:
  -force_dts_monotonicity    Enable monotonicity correction (boolean flag)
  -dts_monotonicity_threshold  Forward jump threshold in microseconds (default: 30s)
  -dts_backward_threshold      Backward jump threshold in microseconds (default: 1s)

IMPORTANT: SCTE-35 streams are explicitly excluded from correction to preserve
scte35ptsadjust BSF accuracy.

